      "value": "I found this in his stomach. It matches Peglaci as well. The remains cannot all be from one individual, as there are three separate left thumbs. So...it seems he was a cannibal. Like the other specimen, there is microscopic writing etched on every millimeter of his entire skeleton. I suspect this is religious text, and that might mean we have stumbled upon what the Peglaci refer to as Ravagers."
